-- FIX-shadow-arity-skew: the #1866 shape reached through the STANDALONE-SHADOW route
-- rather than the ordinary constrained-call route. `size` is this module's own top-level
-- fn AND the name of `Sizeable`'s method, so every occurrence of it is a DEFINER SHADOW
-- and its dicts come from `shadowStandaloneDictSlots`, not from `inferDictAtFound`.
--
-- 🚨 WHY THIS FIXTURE EXISTS. S-slot-key-vector (#1866) re-keyed `dedupSlotVecs` on the
-- WHOLE PREDICATE, so `(Ix a Char, Ix a Bool)` opens TWO dict slots. The DEFINITION side
-- (`expandSupersEntry`, which `dictArityOf` sizes from) picked that up; the shadow route
-- still expanded through `expandSupersPairs`, which pairs every slot with a constant `[]`,
-- and collapsed the two back into ONE. A 1-dict call against a 2-dict definition:
-- measured at sprint head `e19298f5`, `check` exit 0, `run` E-PANIC "intToString: not an
-- Int", `build` exit 0 printing a DIFFERENT heap pointer on every execution, wasm
-- "instantiate failed: illegal cast" -- three engines disagreeing three ways.
--
-- ⚠️ THE SHADOW IS THE FIXTURE. `test/dict_fixtures/s-cardinality-same-iface2.mdk` is this
-- program with the standalone renamed to `useIx` and the `Sizeable` interface removed --
-- byte-comparable, and GREEN throughout the regression. Rename `size` here to a name no
-- interface declares, or delete the `Sizeable` declaration, and this row still passes
-- while testing nothing: the collision with an in-scope method name is what selects the
-- route under test.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER, hand-derived from the declarations before any binary was run:
--   `size 5`  -- both predicates satisfied at `a = Int`: `ix 5 'z'` selects
--              `impl Ix Int Char` = 222 and `ix 5 True` selects `impl Ix Int Bool` = 111,
--              so 333. (444 is the pre-#1866 collapse -- one slot serving both call sites
--              -- and 222 is that collapse landing on the other impl; both are wrong and
--              both are silent.)
--   `plain 5` -- ONE 2-ary predicate, ONE dict slot, 222.
--
-- [T-GLOBAL-TABLE] / review finding F8: `plain` is the FEATURE-PRESENT-PLUS-UNRELATED-
-- CODE-STILL-BEHAVES half this corpus was missing on this route. It is an ordinary
-- non-shadow constrained standalone that never touches `Sizeable` and carries a
-- single-predicate context, so it takes `routesOfMonosTopV`'s scalar arm; its 222 asserts
-- that widening the shadow route's slot list did not perturb the code beside it.
--
-- Section 1 pins both values; section 3 (IRS) pins the two ARITIES -- 2 dicts + 1 value
-- for `size`, 1 dict + 1 value for `plain` -- which no value can see (a call and a
-- definition that agree on the WRONG count print a right-looking number).
interface Sizeable a where
  size : a -> Int

data Box = Box Int

impl Sizeable Box where
  size (Box n) = n

interface Ix a b where
  ix : a -> b -> Int

impl Ix Int Char where
  ix _ _ = 222

impl Ix Int Bool where
  ix _ _ = 111

size : (Ix a Char, Ix a Bool) => a -> Int
size n = ix n 'z' + ix n True

plain : Ix a Char => a -> Int
plain n = ix n 'z'

main =
  let _ = println (size 5)
  println (plain 5)
